wsi/wayland: wait for rendering before presenting when the driver has no implicit sync

Patch 0001 makes the X11 WSI wait for an image's fence on drivers without
implicit sync (Turnip on KGSL). The Wayland WSI did not: Zink's clients under
KWin, and KWin itself presenting to DroidNux's compositor, sent buffers the
GPU was still drawing, and the compositor (then Android, which latches
unsignaled buffers) showed them half rendered: old and new frames mixed,
heavy frames (full resolution) the most. Wait as the X11 WSI does, unless
the swapchain has explicit sync.

--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_wayland.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_wayland.c
@@ -3309,6 +3309,19 @@
    if (chain->retired)
       return VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR;
 
+   /* Without implicit sync (KGSL) and without explicit sync, the compositor
+    * cannot tell when rendering is done: wait for the image's fence, as the
+    * X11 WSI does (patch 0001).
+    */
+   if (chain->base.wsi->no_implicit_sync && !chain->base.image_info.explicit_sync) {
+      MESA_TRACE_SCOPE("wait fence");
+      VkResult result = chain->base.wsi->WaitForFences(chain->base.device, 1,
+                                                       &chain->base.fences[image_index],
+                                                       true, UINT64_MAX);
+      if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
+         return VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR;
+   }
+
    struct wsi_wl_surface *wsi_wl_surface = chain->wsi_wl_surface;
    bool mode_fifo = chain->base.present_mode == VK_PRESENT_MODE_FIFO_KHR;
 
